
<p>10 years ago <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2016/06/10/bitcam">I wrote about BitCam 1.0</a>:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Gorgeous, unbelievably faithful one-bit camera app for iPhone done
in the style of the original Mac. A lovely tribute to <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=bill+atkinson+dithering+algorithm">Bill
Atkinson’s remarkable dithering algorithm</a>. “Catnip for
old-school Mac users,” <a href="https://twitter.com/siracusa/status/740989106268831744">says John Siracusa</a>. Check out <a href="https://twitter.com/cdespinosa/with_replies">the
fun recent-hire-at-Apple Chris Espinosa is having with it</a>.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Originally a creation of The Iconfactory, BitCam is now in the good hands of <a href="https://heliographe.studio/">Héliographe</a> (coiners of <a href="https://www.threads.com/@heliographe.studio/post/DTeOwAykwQ1">the best icon-design zinger</a> ever). Version 2.0 has everything great about BitCam 1, and so much more. Just a wonderful ode to the original Mac, with <a href="https://mastodon.social/@heliographe_studio/117139385118413865">so much</a> <a href="https://mastodon.social/@heliographe_studio/117150743301554818">extraordinary</a> <a href="https://mastodon.social/@heliographe_studio/117149403714856951">attention</a> to detail. Great fun on the iPhone (especially as a camera), and great fun on the Mac (especially to explore the details of its OG-style UI). Free to download on the App Store, and a one-time purchase of just $10 to unlock the full feature set.</p>

<p>If BitCam doesn’t speak to you, you’re not hooked up right.</p>

